when apple announced their new macbooks  we set out to make the best most  comprehensive coverage anywhere on the  internet and we absolutely succeeded and  while doing so we made some  groundbreaking discoveries that nobody  else mentioned or even tested and at the  end of the year we finished off strong  with the final comparison of 2021  and what i found in it really sealed the  deal and made me regret my choice of a  laptop the 14-inch macbook pro with a 2  terabyte ssd 64 gigs of ram and an m1  max processor and in this video i will  tell you exactly why now i know that we  made an utterly insane amount of videos  on these machines so much so that i  myself am sick of them but you have to  admit these videos have and will help  hundreds of thousands of people answer  each and every question that they have  and save money many of them up to a  thousand dollars or more so it was well  worth the effort and for those of you  guys who haven't watched the latest ones  i want to share with you our latest and  final discoveries on the 14-inch macbook  pros and why these are so limited  compared to the 16-inch models despite  apple's marketing i have to start out by  making it very clear that the 14-inch  macbook pros are incredible pieces of  tech when compared to windows machines  and similar form factors as well as the  previous 13-inch macbook pros so if  you're set on this size i don't think  there is any other laptop out there that  offers this mix of features performance  and quality in this form factor no  matter how much money you spend i know  many people who purchase 13-inch macbook  pros over the years despite the  performance being much weaker than the  15 and later on the 16 inch macbooks  just because they love the form factor  in some cases they were their mobile  machines they would come back to a full  desktop and for others they would  connect an egpu to their macbook and  that would become their desktop with  more performance but as you guys know  the apple silicon chips don't support  external graphics cards so buying one  with the right performance matters more  now than ever before and for the first  time ever you can buy the same exact  specifications in a 14 inch macbook as  you can in a 16 inch model all the way  up to 8 terabytes of ssd which used to  be capped at 2 terabytes and 64  gigabytes of unified memory along with  32 graphics cores and an m1 max  processor now i've always been somebody  that loved the smaller macbook pros but  i had to buy the larger models because i  needed the extra cpu cores and the  dedicated graphics but finally in 2021 i  broke that cycle when i decided to  finally ditch the large macbook pro and  go with the 14-inch model a part of that  was the fact that i could get the same  configuration but the bigger thing was  just how large and heavy the big macbook  pros have gotten when apple moved from  the 15-inch model that i really liked to  the 16-inch it got longer wider and  slightly thicker along with almost 10  percent heavier but this year with this  redesign it grew even more than the last  time they changed it and let me tell you  it was significant so much so that it  sealed the deal with me going with a 14  inch macbook pro even though i figured  that it would be slower because of  thermals and i knew that it had worse  battery life i just kept picking this  one up and wanting to use it instead of  the 16 inch model especially when i was  going somewhere well now that it's been  two months and i have used and traveled  with the 14 inch macbook pro and i have  done way more testing and getting  comparisons against other configurations  do i regret buying this 14 inch 4100  macbook pro well like i said earlier  yeah a bit now especially because of my  most recent discovery that absolutely  shocked me ever since our first 14 and  16 inch comparisons we knew just how  huge of a difference there was in the  cooling systems of the smaller and  larger new macbooks the difference is  massive when you put them side by side  the fans look like they are almost twice  the size on the 16 inch and the same  thing goes for the heat pipes and the  fins where the hot air is exhausted this  of course makes sense since the 16 inch  is a lot larger thicker and about 40  percent heavier as well so if you think  about it is actually very impressive  that apple managed or decided to allow  such powerful chips like the m1 max to  be available in the 14 inch model but if  you've been following us for at least a  few years you will know that there is  such a thing as going too far where a  more expensive faster chip will actually  run slower than a cheaper and slower  chip because of thermal throttling now  on the inside we also found that the 14  inch has much smaller speakers in the 16  inch where at apple's event they said  that you get the same exact shockingly  good speaker system in both well i guess  you technically kind of do since both of  them now have six speakers with  dedicated warfares but after using them  side by side i can easily say that the  16-inch system is clearly far better  than the 14 inch with that said the 14  inch beats out most if not all 15 and 16  inch windows laptops and sound quality  but the 16 inch has such deep bass that  i'm still routinely surprised by just  how crazy it sounds with that low bass  that is kind of unbelievable that it's  coming from a laptop it takes movie  watching and music listening to a whole  another level that was impossible before  so after using it and then using my inch  i just know how much better the sound  quality is and what i am missing and it  makes me wish that i decided to lug  around the larger model now before i get  deep into performance i want to talk  about travel we recently went on a trip  and i took my 4100 14 inch maca pro  along with me the size was amazing since  it fits in any backpack or messenger bag  and it fit perfectly on the airplane's  tray table when i was doing some video  editing i have to be honest and say that  i'm really glad that i didn't have a 16  inch laptop it is just too large  especially if the person in front of you  decides to lean back causing you to have  to change the angle of the screen to  something that is almost unusable which  i've had that happened in the past with  my previous 16 inch that was actually  smaller than the current new model the  14 inch is the perfect size for those of  you guys that travel and also need good  performance now as far as battery life  on the other hand well it wasn't great  since i was pushing the machine pretty  hard doing video editing the battery was  draining fairly fast noticeably quicker  than any 13-inch macbook pro macbook air  that i've used to travel in the past now  as you guys know we have done some  battery life comparisons between  different configurations and there is a  startling difference and i want to give  you guys the latest update i use the  same test as luke miani which is using  gfx bench to push the systems pretty  hard simulating really real world tough  testing while at the same time being  able to keep it consistent so we can  actually compare instead of actually  just sitting there doing video editing  which can give you varied results after  just 45 minutes my 32 core 14 inch  dropped down to 52 battery life 12 lower  than the 24 core model while not  actually having that much more  performance due to thermal throttling  now the 24 core scales well in terms  performance from going from a 16 inch  but it only drops about 8 battery which  is quite interesting how well optimized  that model is of course it also runs  hotter since its fans have to work  harder to cool it down which also drains  more battery whereas the 16 core model  runs cooler and has much better battery  but of course less performance so tasks  can take longer jumping to the 16 inch  macbooks with the same test the 32 core  had 64 battery left so 12 more than the  14 inch but what that doesn't show you  is the fact that the 16 inch is much  more powerful as well being about 30  percent faster in tough gpu tests which  is a huge performance increase and even  though it uses more power and it runs  the gpu at the full 1300 megahertz  instead of about a thousand megahertz or  so for this task or even lower if it's  thermal throttling more the battery life  is still much better now of course you  can hook up a nice portable battery pack  to juice up your 14 inch and supplement  its battery that is about 40 percent  smaller than the 16 inch and that is  exactly what i did on the airplane in  regular daily use one thing you can't do  is get the extra performance difference  back i know some of you guys told me to  manually preset the fans higher to cool  down the 14 inch and i did try that but  it really doesn't make any difference  the system still heats up just as fast  and for the brief time that it runs cool  apple still artificially limits the  graphics to a maximum of 1100 megahertz  instead of the full 1300 megahertz on  the 16 inch what really got me though is  when i did my ultimate gpu comparison  and i pushed the machines hard in the  2500 base 16-inch macbook pro performed  practically the same as my 4100  14-inch that has double the graphics  cores and four times the memory um and  not only that that 16 inch model also  ran much cooler and almost silent  whereas this 14 inch was blasting its  fans at full blast this really sealed  the deal for me just knowing that my  expensive 14-inch macbook pro is the  worst value new macbook pro that is out  there now i knew that it would thermal  throttle and it would have worse battery  but not by this much and after a few  months of testing it and using it  knowing just how much better the 16-inch  macbook pros are it is really a bummer  the apple's 14-inch is limited both  thermally because it's smaller as well  as artificially because apple is locking  down the graphics performance even if  you're plugged into power  and your system is running cool it is  crazy that the 16 inch base model can  even outperform it in some tough cases  i really think that apple should give  this 14 inch the high power mode that  the 16 inch macbook pro has because it  is actually useful for this machine  allowing it to reach its full  performance if your battery is good and  the system isn't already preheated up  and running really hot in thermal  throttling now at this point while i  really like the 14 inch form factor i'm  going to try to get over that  extra size and weight just because i  know how much of a better value the 16  inch model is costing just 200 more but  giving you more value better thermals  quieter fans better performance overall  and way better battery life as well and  you can actually save money and get a  weaker spec  but overall have better performance than  using a 14-inch machine so overall do i  regret getting this expensive 14-inch i  think so and i think if i got maybe the  24 core even more of the base model it  provides a way better value and a much  more optimized system as far as the  performance in the form factor compared  to this 32 core m1 max you guys let me  know your opinions if you're somebody  that bought a max out 14 inch what is  your experience been like and did you  expect it to be slower than a much  cheaper 16 inch i just want to get all  that latest info out there for you guys  that didn't watch the latest comparisons  it really is a shocker and some stuff  that nobody really talks about or even  tested so i'm glad that we could do that  for you guys go ahead and click that  circle above to subscribe and help us  reach our goal of 1 million subscribers  we would greatly appreciate it and check  out one of those great videos right over  there this has been max and i will see  you in the next video  [Music]

